[test-suite name=xap-dist
  [doc [#
Conformance fixtures for XAP feature distribution — the §6.1 P0 function
surface of spec/02-working/xap_feature_distribution_market.md (P0 subset of the
§11 list): pkg-tree (canonical content document), pkg-seal / pkg-sign
(publisher side), pkg-publish / pkg-fetch (alias = name for a manifest hash,
immutable once released), pkg-verify (the §3 fail-closed chain), pkg-install
(fetch → verify → per-kind gate → consent=grants → enable), and
pkg-requires-closure (the code plane, hash-pinned).

Keypairs/DIDs are generated fresh per case (entropy), so assertions project
STABLE fields (status, names, counts, aliases, error codes) — never random
hashes/DIDs. Content-tree hashes ARE deterministic (canonical form) and two
puts of the same set must agree (001).

CXER4881 (present-but-divergent content) is deliberately not fixtured: an
honest content-addressed store cannot produce it (get-doc(H) re-renders to H
by construction) — it guards dishonest mirrors and is defense-in-depth behind
the store's own CXER1120. The absent-content stage is 4886 (010).

The nmea0183 case (016) reads the REAL packaged codec source from
packages/nmea0183/nmea0183.cx (repo-root-relative, the runner's process CWD
contract) — the distribution pipeline is dogfooded on the actual first
kind=library package, not a toy.

Case 025 (§11.15, stage-1 half) consumes the COMMITTED registry/ store — a
git-repo-as-registry (§4.1): full hash + publisher-DID signature verification
against committed bytes, no service running. Its pinned hashes are the §7
supply-chain witness: they are stable forever because a released artifact is
immutable (a codec change is a NEW version; nmea0183@0.1.0 never moves).
#]]

  [case id=xap-dist-001-tree-canonical-order level=core
   [tags xap-dist pkg-tree canonical determinism]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-xap' :as xap]
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/store' :as store]
[?let [= $s [$store:open "mem://"]]
 [= $t1 [$xap:pkg-tree ([entry path='b.cx' 'bee'], [entry path='a.cx' 'ay'])]]
 [= $t2 [$xap:pkg-tree ([entry path='a.cx' 'ay'], [entry path='b.cx' 'bee'])]]
 [= [$store:put-doc $s $t1] [$store:put-doc $s $t2]]]
#]]
   [out-text [#
true
#]]
  ]

  [case id=xap-dist-002-tree-traversal-path-rejected level=core
   [tags xap-dist pkg-tree path fail-closed]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-xap' :as xap]
[$xap:pkg-tree ([entry path='../evil.cx' 'x'])]
#]]
   [out-err [#
cx-err:CXER4880
#]]
  ]

  [case id=xap-dist-003-tree-duplicate-path-rejected level=core
   [tags xap-dist pkg-tree path fail-closed]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-xap' :as xap]
[$xap:pkg-tree ([entry path='a.cx' 'one'], [entry path='a.cx' 'two'])]
#]]
   [out-err [#
cx-err:CXER4880
#]]
  ]

  [case id=xap-dist-004-seal-pins-tree-hash level=core
   [tags xap-dist pkg-seal tier1]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-xap' :as xap]
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/store' :as store]
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/crypto' :as crypto]
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/did' :as did]
[?let [= $s [$store:open "mem://"]]
 [= $kp [$crypto:ed25519-keypair]]
 [= $pub [$did:key-create $kp@public]]
 [= $tree [$xap:pkg-tree ([entry path='lib.cx' 'code'], [entry path='package.cxd' 'm'])]]
 [= $draft [?element "package"
                      [?attr "name" "toylib"] [?attr "version" "0.1.0"] [?attr "kind" "library"]
                  [?element "publisher" [?attr "did" $pub]]
                  [?element "exports" [?element "def" [?attr "name" "toylib/id"]]]]]
 [= $sealed [$xap:pkg-seal $s $tree $draft]]
 [= $th [$store:put-doc $s $tree]]
 [= $sealed@hash $th]]
#]]
   [out-text [#
true
#]]
  ]

  [case id=xap-dist-005-seal-library-needs-rejected level=core
   [tags xap-dist pkg-seal n-dist-2 fail-closed]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-xap' :as xap]
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/store' :as store]
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/crypto' :as crypto]
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/did' :as did]
[?let [= $s [$store:open "mem://"]]
 [= $kp [$crypto:ed25519-keypair]]
 [= $pub [$did:key-create $kp@public]]
 [= $tree [$xap:pkg-tree ([entry path='lib.cx' 'code'])]]
 [= $draft [?element "package"
                      [?attr "name" "toylib"] [?attr "version" "0.1.0"] [?attr "kind" "library"]
                  [?element "publisher" [?attr "did" $pub]]
                  [?element "exports" [?element "def" [?attr "name" "toylib/id"]]]
                  [?element "needs" [?element "reads" [?attr "noun" "traffic/vessel"]]]]]
 [$xap:pkg-seal $s $tree $draft]]
#]]
   [out-err [#
cx-err:CXER4880
#]]
  ]

